  "worked_solution": "The condition after the \"$:$\" symbol\n\n$$\nn\\in Z,\\,n\\le 4\n$$\n\nstates that $n$ can be any integer number that satisfies the inequality $-2\\le n\\le 2.$ In other words, \n\n$$\nn={-2,-1,0,1,2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elements of $B$ are all the terms of the sequence ${b}_{n},$ given by\n\n$$\n{b}_{n}={n}^{3}-4,\\,n\\in {-2,-1,0,1,2}.\n$$\n\nLet's write down all the terms of our sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{-2} & =(-2)^{3}-4=-8-4=-12 \\\\ {b}_{-1} & =(-1)^{3}-4=-1-4=-5 \\\\ {b}_{0} & ={0}^{3}-4=0-4=-4 \\\\ {b}_{1} & ={1}^{3}-4=1-4=-3 \\\\ {b}_{2} & ={2}^{3}-4=8-4=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nB={-12,-5,-4,-3,4}.\n$$",
